   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome-level indicators
1.1. No. of small holders/farmers provided with improved access to irrigation infrastructure (disaggregated by gender)
1.2. Increase in agriculture production in the project area (ton/year)
1.3.	Increase in key crop yields (cotton, wheat, fruits and vegetables) 
1.4.	Percentage increase in aggregate of key crop yields (cotton, wheat, fruits and vegetables)
1.5.	No. of jobs created on on-farm and off-farm level
1.6.	No. of people provided with access to improved water for domestic use (gender disaggregated)
1.7.	No. of people provided with access to improved sanitation facilities (gender disaggregated)
1.8.	Increase in water supply network efficiency (%) 
a. No. of new Shariah compliant financial products launched; 
b. No. of financial institutions received license to run Shariah compliant operations

Output-level indicators
Output 1:
1.1. No. of irrigation and drainage service providers (Raivodkhozes) covered with capacity building support on - (a) Financial Management, (b) Technical and Operational Management, and (c) Institutional Management. 
1.2. No. of Water Users Associations (WUAs) provided with capacity building support on - (a) Financial Management, (b) Technical and Operational Management, and (c) Institutional Management.
1.3. No. of people trained on - (a) Financial Management, (b) Technical and Operational Management, and (c) Institutional Management. (Gender disaggregated) 
1.4. No. of tariff and billing collection system established 

Output 2:
2.1. No. of water supply and sewerage service providers (SUE KMK, Vodokanals, Tojikobdehot, alternative models if feasible) provided with capacity building support on - (a) Financial Management, (b) Technical and Operational Management, and (c) Institutional Management.
2.2. No. of people  trained on - (a) Financial Management, (b) Technical and Operational Management, and (c) Institutional Management. (Gender disaggregated)
2.3. No. of tariff and billing collection system established</narrative>
    </description>
