    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1. Project Inception Phase initiated.
1.2. Stakeholder consultations held with key counterparts and development partners on the approach to implement interventions on irrigation &amp; drainage, drinking water supply and sewerage, and sanitation &amp; hygiene.
1.3. Preliminary data collected on the (i) Irrigation &amp; Drainage, (ii) Drinking Water Supply and Sewerage, and (iii) Sanitation and Hygiene.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1. During the reporting period between August &#x2013; December 2022, UNDP had implemented necessary preparatory activities towards initiating the project Inception Phase. Detailed work plan was drafted, and overall implementation strategy was agreed with principal project partners &#x2013; Agency for Land Reclamation and Irrigation (ALRI), Project Implementation Unit &#x201c;Danghara Valley Irrigation Project&#x201d; (PIU DVIP) and the Islamic Development Bank (IsDB). The Inception period is expected to be concluded in January-February 2023 with the organization of the Inception Workshop and finalization of the Inception Report. 
1.2. Stakeholder consultations were held with key development partners active in areas as relevant to project interventions. The consultations/reviews were conducted on the approaches towards implementing IWRM-based sector reform by the WB, SDC, EU, ADB across all river basins in Tajikistan, with the involvement of national government agencies (MoEWR, ALRI) during relevant coordination meetings. 
1.3. Preliminary data was collected on all components &#x2013; (i) Irrigation &amp; Drainage, (ii) Drinking Water Supply and Sewerage, and (iii) Sanitation and Hygiene &#x2013; through the desk review, consultations with ALRI and joint field mission to the target districts of Khatlon District. The data obtained will be further used for defining actual targets, indicators, stakeholder engagement plans, and preliminary needs and gaps for institutional strengthening with regards to WUA, ALRI departments and SUE KMK.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
